  ],
  "slug": "development-use-disease-pathogenesis-4e25",
  "summary": "Single-cell transcriptomics is now routinely coupled with Mendelian randomization and network pharmacology to nominate causal and druggable candidates.",
  "synthesis": "Most items pair single-cell transcriptomics with a second evidence layer to rank candidate targets, using network pharmacology or toxicology, machine-learning feature selection, docking, molecular dynamics, or Mendelian randomization with colocalization. Examples include monocyte PRKCB-CTSL in rheumatoid arthritis, LIPA and LTA4H in vitiligo, GM2A and SLC15A2 in psoriasis, and Rora-regulon granulosa cells in PCOS. Two studies apply in silico perturbation: single-cell perturbation of Turmeric-Pueraria-Coix polyphenols and scTenifoldKnk virtual knockout of CYP1B1 in renal fibrosis. The butyrate RNA-seq preprint, sepsis m6A profiling, and somatotropinoma proteomics are bulk-level and lack this pipeline. Target lists remain predictive rather than mechanistically established.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-25"
}
